  "headline": "Indonesian Police Confirm Listyo Sigit Cannot Resign Amid Treason Case",
  "seoTitle": "Listyo Sigit Treason Case and Indonesia Police Resignation",
  "metaDescription": "Indonesian authorities confirm former police chief Listyo Sigit cannot resign due to ongoing investigations into alleged treason and wiretapping activities.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Police officials state Listyo Sigit is ineligible to resign while facing criminal allegations and potential code of ethics violations.",
    "Investigations are ongoing regarding claims of unauthorized wiretapping of the President and involvement in alleged treasonous activities.",
    "The Coordinating Minister for Political and Security Affairs has commented on the alleged motives behind the actions attributed to the former police chief."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police has officially stated that former National Police Chief Listyo Sigit is prohibited from resigning from his post. Officials cited legal regulations, noting that officers facing criminal threats exceeding five years or those involved in code of ethics investigations are ineligible to step down or retire honorably. The former police chief is currently the subject of a high-profile investigation regarding his alleged involvement in wiretapping the President and organizing large-scale demonstrations interpreted by authorities as treason. The case has drawn significant attention from both local media and international outlets. Furthermore, Coordinating Minister for Political and Security Affairs Dudung Abdurachman has publicly addressed the suspected motives behind these activities. President Prabowo Subianto has reportedly instructed security agencies, including the police and the State Intelligence Agency, to thoroughly investigate the allegations surrounding the case.",
